App 30: The Counterfactual Explorer
Completeness status: COMPLETE. All sections delivered in one pass. No truncation. Formatted for copy-paste. Long lists are broken into short lines.

1. What It Is
A tool that takes a model and a proposed intervention, and explores what happens under different conditions. It lets a user specify a model, specify an intervention on a term, a coupling, a parameter, or a sub-system, run the intervention, and record the outcome. It records the counterfactual dependence of the outcome on the intervention, the material-change test, and the relation to the standard model.

It reuses:

the STAG Annotation Editor (App 1)

the Full-Pipeline Simulator (App 9)

the STAG Schema Library (App 17)

the Null-Model Protocol Library (App 18)

the STAG plus Null-Model Combined Workbench (App 14)

the Provenance-Aware Annotation Database (App 20)

the Numerical Verification Tool (App 22)

the Physics Knowledge Library (App 23)

the Autofill Library Service (App 49)

It is for theoreticians, experimentalists, and anyone who asks the question "what if this contribution were removed?"

2. Core Requirements
Functional requirements:

Accept a model specification from the user.

Accept an intervention specification from the user.

Accept the outcome measure and the material-change test.

Run the intervention.

Record the outcome under the intervention and the outcome without the intervention.

Record the difference between the two outcomes.

Apply the material-change test and record the result.

Classify the counterfactual dependence.

Record the provenance.

Link to a STAG annotation if the intervention is part of a scale-transition claim.

Link to a Null-Model Protocol result if the intervention is tested statistically.

Link to a numerical verification result if the reported numbers have been verified.

Link to a Physics Knowledge Library work if the model is described in a deposited work.

Enforce provenance completeness.

Enforce versioning.

Enforce supersession acyclicity.

Support querying by counterfactual ID, model reference, intervention kind, outcome measure, dependence classification, depositor, deposit date, and keywords.

Support full-text search of the description, the intervention, and the notes.

Support aggregation queries: count by model, by intervention kind, by dependence classification, by year, by depositor.

Support exporting a counterfactual as JSON, PROV-O, and Turtle.

Support importing a counterfactual from JSON.

Support bulk import and bulk export.

Support a REST API for CRUD operations.

Support a GraphQL API for flexible queries.

Support a command-line interface for administration.

Support authentication and authorization.

Support audit logging.

Support backup and restore.

Support a web interface.

Support moderation.

Support the intervention comparison view: a visualisation that compares two or more interventions on the same model.

Support the counterfactual map: a visualisation of the interventions on a model and their outcomes.

Non-functional requirements:

Deterministic.

Fast: query a typical counterfactual in under 100 milliseconds.

Scalable: support up to 10^6 counterfactuals.

Versioned: the explorer records the STAG schema version, the Null-Model Protocol schema version, the counterfactual schema version, and the explorer version.

Reproducible.

Portable.

Well-documented.

