6. Full Counterfactual Specification
6.1 Counterfactual Schema
The counterfactual schema defines the structure of a counterfactual deposit.

It has the following fields:

counterfactual_id. A string. Required.

model_reference. A string. Required.

model_parameters. An object. Required.

intervention. An object. Required. It contains intervention_kind, intervention_target, and intervention_description.

intervention_kind. An enum. The values are boundary_term, defining_coupling, subdominant_coupling, parameter_change, subsystem_removal, other.

outcome_measure. An object. Required. It contains measure_name, measure_units, and measure_description.

outcome_without_intervention. An object. Required. It contains value and uncertainty.

outcome_with_intervention. An object. Required. It contains value and uncertainty.

outcome_change. An object. Required. It contains absolute_change, relative_change, and direction.

material_change_test. An object. Required. It contains test_type, test_parameters, and test_justification.

material_change_result. An enum. The values are material, not_material, uncertain, not_determinable.

dependence_classification. An enum. The values are yes, no, definitional_only, untestable, uncertain, not_determinable.

quantities_held_fixed. An array of strings. Required.

provenance. An object. Required.

stag_annotation. An object. Optional.

null_model_result. An object. Optional.

numerical_verification_result. An object. Optional.

work_reference. A string. Optional.

keywords. An array of strings. Optional.

notes. A string. Optional.

moderation_status. An enum. The values are pending, approved, rejected.

version. An integer.

supersedes. A string. Optional.

superseded_by. A string. Optional.

