7. Core Logic as Executable Pseudocode
7.1 Create Counterfactual
function createCounterfactual(counterfactual, files, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Validate the counterfactual against the schema. If invalid, return an error with the details.

Step 3. If the STAG annotation is present, validate it.

Step 4. If the Null-Model Protocol result is present, validate it.

Step 5. If the verification result is present, validate it.

Step 6. If the work reference is present, look it up. If null, flag it as unresolved.

Step 7. Generate a counterfactual ID. Set the fields: version 1, moderation_status pending, deposit_date now, depositor_id from auth, depositor_affiliation from auth, provenance from provenance.

Step 8. Insert the counterfactual.

Step 9. Insert the STAG link, the Null-Model link, the verification link, and the work link if present.

Step 10. Insert the provenance.

Step 11. Insert the moderation record.

Step 12. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 13. Return the counterfactual_id and the status created.

7.2 Run Intervention
function runIntervention(modelReference, modelParameters, intervention, outcomeMeasure, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. If the model is analytic, evaluate the outcome without the intervention and the outcome with the intervention directly.

Step 3. If the model requires simulation, call App 9 (Full-Pipeline Simulator) with the model parameters and the intervention as the alternative.

Step 4. Collect the outcome without the intervention and the outcome with the intervention.

Step 5. Compute the outcome change.

Step 6. Apply the material-change test.

Step 7. Classify the dependence.

Step 8. Return the outcome without the intervention, the outcome with the intervention, the outcome change, the material-change result, and the dependence classification.

7.3 Read Counterfactual
function readCounterfactual(counterfactualId, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "reader"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the counterfactual. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Read the links, the provenance, and the moderation.

Step 4. Reconstruct the deposit.

Step 5. Insert the audit log entry.

Step 6. Return the deposit.

7.4 Update Counterfactual
function updateCounterfactual(counterfactualId, counterfactual, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "depositor"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing counterfactual. If null, return an error.

Step 3. Validate the new counterfactual.

Step 4. Increment the version. Update the supersedes and superseded_by fields.

Step 5. Insert a provenance record with operation update.

Step 6. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 7. Return the counterfactual_id, the version, and the status updated.

7.5 Delete Counterfactual
function deleteCounterfactual(counterfactualId, provenance, auth):

Step 1. validateAuth(auth, "admin"). If not authorized, return an error.

Step 2. Read the existing counterfactual. If null, return an error.

Step 3. If soft delete, mark as deleted. Otherwise, remove.

Step 4. Insert an audit log entry.

Step 5. Return the counterfactual_id and the status deleted.

